{"type":"text","timestamp":1788512129825,"sessionID":"ses_f94670cb8ffeWdbpzRFsoZCXEH","part":{"id":"prt_06ba13d7a001K11L0Ta0KNX1sQ","messageID":"msg_06ba1378f001jKS8MY7oKKQ4yy","sessionID":"ses_f94670cb8ffeWdbpzRFsoZCXEH","type":"text","text":"Done. `conanws.yml` now uses a list-of-packages format, implemented across 4 source files (+ test updates), all 39 workspace integration tests pass.\n\n**`conan/internal/model/workspace.py`**\n- `add()` (conan/internal/model/workspace.py:44): appends `{\"path\": ..., \"ref\": str(ref), [\"output_folder\": ...]}` entries to the `packages` list; warns `\"Package <path> already exists, skipping\"` and skips duplicates by path\n- `remove()` (conan/internal/model/workspace.py:57): matches by normalized unix path, returns the path; clear error `\"No editable package to remove from this path\"` when missing (I added a `next(..., None)` default over upstream so this raises `ConanException` instead of `StopIteration`)\n- `clean()` (conan/internal/model/workspace.py:68): labels each editable by `ref` if defined, otherwise by path\n- `packages()`: returns a list\n\n**`conan/api/subapi/workspace.py`** — `packages()` (conan/api/subapi/workspace.py:106) now iterates list entries, deduces the reference from the `ref` field or by loading the conanfile (name/version/user/channel), validates it, and errors on: missing conanfile (`Workspace editable not found`), non-deducible/invalid refs (`Workspace editable reference could not be deduced by <path>/conanfile.py...`), and duplicate refs (`Workspace editable reference '<ref>' already exists.`)\n\n**`conan/cli/commands/workspace.py`** — `workspace info` text formatter (conan/cli/commands/workspace.py:96) renders each package as `- path: ...` with an indented `ref: ...` line when a reference exists (`(empty)` when none); JSON format returns the raw list entries\n\n**`conan/internal/api/new/workspace.py`** — the `conan new workspace` template now emits the list format with explicit `path`/`ref` fields\n\nVerified end-to-end: template generation, add-dedupe, remove-by-path, clean messaging (ref-based when available, path fallback), and all error paths. The only failing tests (`test_export_read_only`, functional `test_metabuild`) fail identically on clean HEAD due to environment limitations (root user / CMake version), unrelated to this change.","time":{"start":1788512124282,"end":1788512129819}}}
